From bea85a42966cf1e1bc0810a1ad7034d3f7ab5091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:29:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(post): Agie Wire EDM posts reentrant line and arc
 openings

A Wire Contour with the side Die on one selected closed DXF chain now
posts through the Agie Wire EDM (AgieVision) post. The ISO keeps the
nominal walls counter-clockwise from the seam with G01, G02 and G03 and
incremental I/J; the SBL is the zero-step die setup (c_die).

The post refuses by name, with the values: unequal arc radii on the
grid, an inside fillet of the plate not larger than the rough offset
(0.245 mm), a joint at an arc without a common tangent, a sharp inside
plate corner past the 0.002 mm cover rest, walls closer than two rough
passes and wire, a hole or lead too near a wall, and too little stock.

The app reads the placed walls with the inspection export's code, now
shared in operation/agie_opening.rs. Imported on an offline copy of the
control software: REENT20 passed FORMALCHECK with the expected passes.

Fixes #3178

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
